Design decisions for per-replica CMEK (issue #6317):

- Kept the field name replicationLocations rather than adding a new
  "replicas" field; the type changed from []string to
  []PushSecretReplica with a custom UnmarshalJSON that accepts both
  plain location strings (existing metadata keeps parsing) and
  {location, cmekKeyName} objects. sigs.k8s.io/yaml converts YAML to
  JSON first, so encoding/json hooks apply.
- The alias-type trick in UnmarshalJSON is mandatory: decoding into the
  receiver's own type recurses into UnmarshalJSON forever (stack
  overflow caught in tests). The string branch rejects empty/null
  entries; the object branch rejects unknown fields and empty location.
- A CMEK key used alone (no replicationLocations) with automatic
  replication must come from the "global" multi-region per GCP docs;
  validateGlobalCMEKKeyName enforces this. The validation is skipped
  for regional SecretStores (buildReplication takes regionalStore)
  because regional secrets carry no replication at all - the key is
  applied through the regional endpoint. First review draft missed
  this: it hard-failed the documented regional-store + regional-key
  pattern. Regression test in client_test.go covers it.
- Per-replica key inheritance from top-level cmekKeyName is only valid
  when the inherited key matches the replica location (GCP: user-managed
  replica keys must map exactly to the replica location); docs carry a
  caveat instead of code validation, per user decision.
- buildReplication copies the parsed spec before mutating entries to
  avoid aliasing the caller's metadata.
- Regional secrets (store.Location != "") never receive replication in
  the create path; the regional update path is untouched.
